  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nSurface high pressure will remain in place across the central \nAppalachians into this weekend. This will provide for dry conditions\nand seasonably warm daytime highs for our area. \n\nWith good radiational cooling, will likely see areas of river \nvalley fog again later tonight into early Thursday morning. Will \nalso continue to undercut overnight lows the next couple of nights \nand lower afternoon dewpoints from guidance. \n\nA cold front will move through late in the weekend. This will bring \nthe next chance for precipitation, along with cooler temperatures \nfor early next week.",
